).\n\nThe perpendicular bisector of \\(BF\\) passes through  \n\n\\[\nM_{BF}= \\Bigl(\\frac{-0.20+2.236}{2},\\;\\frac{-2.994+5.326}{2}\\Bigr)\n      \\approx(1.018,\\;1.166)\n\\]\n\nand has slope  \n\n\\[\nm_{2}= \\dfrac{-(x_{F}-x_{B})}{y_{F}-y_{B}}\n      =\\dfrac{-2.436}{8.320}\\approx-0.293 .\n\\]\n\nSolving the two linear equations yields the intersection point\n\n\\[\nO\\approx(1.294,\\;1.084).\n\\]\n\nThe circum‑radius is  \n\n\\[\nR_{BEF}=|OB| \\approx \\sqrt{(1.294+0.20)^{2}+(1.084+2.994)^{2}}\n        \\approx 4.344 .\n\\]\n\n---\n\n### 6.  The line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\)\n\nThe direction vector of \\(AP\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AP}=P-A\\approx(4.20,\\;4.020).\n\\]\n\nThe line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is  \n\n\\[\n\\ell_{H}:\\; (x,y)=H+s\\,\\overrightarrow{AP},\\qquad s\\in\\mathbb R .\n\\]\n\nThe (perpendicular) distance from the centre \\(O\\) to this line is\n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}\\bigl(O,\\ell_{H}\\bigr)\n   =\\frac{\\bigl|\\overrightarrow{AP}\\times (O-H)\\bigr|}\n          {\\|\\overrightarrow{AP}\\|}\n   =\\frac{|\\,4.20\\,(1.084-0.570)-4.020\\,(1.294-4)\\,|}\n          {\\sqrt{4.20^{2}+4.020^{2}}}\n   \\approx\\frac{13.041}{5.815}\n   \\approx 2.244 .\n\\]\n\nSince  \n\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dist}\\bigl(O,\\ell_{H}\\bigr)=2.244\\neq R_{BEF}=4.344,\n\\]\n\nthe line \\(\\ell_{H}\\) does **not** touch the circle \\((BEF)\\); it meets the circle in two points.\n\n---\n\n### 7.  Conclusion\n\nFor the explicit configuration chosen above the line through the orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\) that is parallel to \\(AP\\) is **not** tangent to the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).  \nHence the statement “the line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\) is tangent to the circumcircle of \\(BEF\\)” is **false** in general. ∎"
