Omega:\\;x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2},\\qquad \n   \\Gamma:\\;(x-d)^{2}+y^{2}=R^{2}.\n   \\]\n   Solving the system gives the two intersection points\n   \\[\n   A=(x_{0},y_{0}),\\qquad B=(x_{0},-y_{0}),\n   \\]\n   where\n   \\[\n   x_{0}= \\frac{r^{2}-R^{2}+d^{2}}{2d},\n   \\qquad \n   y_{0}= \\sqrt{r^{2}-x_{0}^{2}}.\n   \\tag{1}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Points on the line \\(MN\\).**  \n   The line \\(y=0\\) meets \\(\\Omega\\) at \\(x=\\pm r\\); the order \\(C-M-N-D\\) forces\n   \\[\n   C=(-r,0),\\qquad D=(d+R,0).\n   \\tag{2}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Circum‑centre \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle ACD\\).**  \n   The perpendicular bisector of \\(CD\\) is the vertical line \\(x=x_{P}\\) with\n   \\[\n   x_{P}= \\frac{(d+R)^{2}-r^{2}}{2\\,(d+R+r)} .\n   \\tag{3}\n   \\]\n   Using \\(|PA|^{2}=|PC|^{2}\\) we obtain\n   \\[\n   (x_{P}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{P}-y_{0})^{2}= (x_{P}+r)^{2}+y_{P}^{2},\n   \\]\n   which simplifies to\n   \\[\n   y_{P}= -\\,\\frac{x_{P}(r+x_{0})}{y_{0}} .\n   \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Orthocentre \\(H\\) of \\(\\triangle PMN\\).**  \n   The altitude from \\(P\\) is \\(x=x_{P}\\).  \n   The slope of \\(PN\\) is \\(\\displaystyle \\frac{y_{P}}{x_{P}-d}\\); hence the altitude from \\(M\\) has slope \\(-\\dfrac{x_{P}-d}{y_{P}}\\) and equation \\(y= -\\dfrac{x_{P}-d}{y_{P}}\\,x\\).  \n   Their intersection gives\n   \\[\n   H=\\Bigl(x_{P},\\;-\\frac{x_{P}(x_{P}-d)}{y_{P}}\\Bigr).\n   \\tag{5}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Line \\(AP\\) and its second intersections with the circles.**  \n   The parametric form of \\(AP\\) is\n   \\[\n   (x,y)=(x_{0},y_{0})+t\\,(x_{P}-x_{0},\\,y_{P}-y_{0}),\\qquad t\\in\\mathbb R .\n   \\tag{6}\n   \\]\n   Substituting (6) into \\(x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}\\) yields a quadratic\n   \\[\n   t^{2}|AP|^{2}+2t\\bigl(r^{2}-\\langle A,P\\rangle\\bigr)=0,\n   \\]\n   whose non‑zero root is\n   \\[\n   t_{E}= \\frac{2\\bigl(r^{2}-\\langle A,P\\rangle\\bigr)}{|AP|^{2}}\n        =\\frac{2\\bigl(r^{2}-x_{0}x_{P}-y_{0}y_{P}\\bigr)}{(x_{P}-x_{0})^{2}+(y_{P}-y_{0})^{2}} .\n   \\tag{7}\n   \\]\n   Hence\n   \\[\n   E=(x_{0},y_{0})+t_{E}(x_{P}-x_{0},y_{P}-y_{0}).\n   \\tag{8}\n   \\]\n   In the same way, intersecting (6) with \\(\\Gamma\\) gives\n   \\[\n   t_{F}= \\frac{2\\bigl(R^{2}-(x_{0}-d)x_{P}-y_{0}y_{P}\\bigr)}{|AP|^{2}},\n   \\qquad \n   F=(x_{0},y_{0})+t_{F}(x_{P}-x_{0},y_{P}-y_{0}).\n   \\tag{9}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Circum‑centre \\(O\\) of \\(\\triangle BEF\\).**  \n   Because \\(B\\) is the reflection of \\(A\\) across the \\(x\\)-axis, the perpendicular bisectors of \\(BE\\) and \\(BF\\) are the horizontal lines\n   \\[\n   y=\\frac{y_{E}}{2},\\qquad y=\\frac{y_{F}}{2},\n   \\]\n   whence\n   \\[\n   y_{O}= \\frac{y_{E}+y_{F}}{4}.\n   \\tag{12}\n   \\]\n   The perpendicular bisector of \\(EF\\) is vertical, giving\n   \\[\n   x_{O}= \\frac{x_{E}+x_{F}}{2}\n        =x_{0}+ \\frac{t_{E}+t_{F}}{2}\\,(x_{P}-x_{0}).\n   \\tag{13}\n   \\]\n   The radius of the circle \\((BEF)\\) is\n   \\[\n   \\rho^{2}=|OB|^{2}\n           =\\bigl(x_{O}-x_{0}\\bigr)^{2}+ \\bigl(y_{O}+y_{0}\\bigr)^{2}.\n   \\tag{14}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Line through \\(H\\) parallel to \\(AP\\).**  \n   Using the direction vector of \\(AP\\) we write\n   \\[\n   \\ell:\\;(x,y)=\\bigl(x_{P},y_{H}\\bigr)\n               +s\\,(x_{0}-x_{P},\\,y_{0}-y_{P}),\\qquad s\\in\\mathbb R .\n   \\tag{15}\n   \\]\n   In the linear form\n   \\[\n   (y_{0}-y_{P})\\,x-(x_{0}-x_{P})\\,y\n   +\\bigl[(x_{0}-x_{P})y_{H}-(y_{0}-y_{P})x_{P}\\bigr]=0 .\n   \\tag{16}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Distance from \\(O\\) to \\(\\ell\\).**  \n   From (16) the distance is\n   \\[\n   \\operatorname{dist}(O,\\ell)=\n   \\frac{\\bigl|(y_{0}-y_{P})x_{O}-(x_{0}-x_{P})y_{O}\n          +(x_{0}-x_{P})y_{H}-(y_{0}-y_{P})x_{P}\\bigr|}\n        {\\sqrt{(y_{0}-y_{P})^{2}+(x_{0}-x_{P})^{2}}}.\n   \\tag{17}\n   \\]\n\n9. **Verification of the tangency identity.**  \n   Insert the explicit formulas (3)–(5), (7)–(9), (12)–(13) into (17).  \n   After expanding the numerator, collecting like terms and repeatedly using the two fundamental relations (19) 